(Tessera) title
(System architecture and feature review) subtitle
rule
(Executive narrative) h
(Tessera is a durable research-control workspace, not a generic agent shell or a compute scheduler.) t
(Its intended value is a traceable path from a goal through a bounded experiment and evidence to a) t
(human decision. The repository implements meaningful slices of that path: local control records,) t
(immutable plans, scoped credentials, execution admission, durable ledgers, a sandboxed desktop shell,) t
(CPU supervision, artifact quarantine, recovery, and narrowly fenced coordinator and Kubernetes seams.) t
(The review finds a deliberately conservative architecture: authority is centered in the control plane;) t
(the desktop, Astra coordinator, OpenCode, workers, and Kubernetes adapters are clients or constrained) t
(effectors. This is a strong shape for honest research records, but it is not yet a complete pilot.) t
rule
(Bottom line) sh
(Implemented components create, retain, and display bounded records. Synthetic and opt-in fixtures) t
(exercise selected seams. Real provider execution, supported remote control, selected OpenCode) t
(compatibility, Kubernetes target attachment, artifact release, result acceptance, and scientific) t
(validation remain absent or explicitly gated. No test count or component pass is treated here as a) t
(live experiment, provider-billing, laptop-independence, or scientific-success claim.) t
rule
(Snapshot and evidence caveat) h
(Review date: 14 September 2026. Repository snapshot: main at 6668ab8, before this review artifact.) t
(The working tree was intentionally dirty: 65 tracked paths modified, 27 untracked paths, 92 entries) t
(total; no staged paths. The uncommitted Astra, remote-workflow, provisioner, script, desktop, control,) t
(worker, documentation, and test work was inspected as repository content, not represented as merged.) t
(Current source constant: schema v43 in src/tessera_control/migrations.py. README and implementation-) t
(progress text still describe the historical schema-v42 evidence checkpoint; those claims are preserved) t
(as dated historical evidence, not silently upgraded. Schema v43 adds operation-bound remote workflow) t
(lifecycle records for new packages only: heartbeat, opaque checkpoint, reconnect/outage observations.) t
(It does not prove a run, provider termination, replacement submission, held-restore writability, or) t
(laptop independence.) t
rule
(Scope and method) sh
(Read DESIGN.md, README.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, decisions, major control/worker/provisioner/agent and) t
(desktop packages, migrations/recovery, Kubernetes/OpenCode/live-E2E/setup/conformance scripts, tests,) t
(and the current diff. This is an architecture review of source and documented evidence; no screenshots,) t
(secrets, credentials, application-code edits, provider calls, Docker/Kubernetes live runs, or commits.) t
