(Authority labels) h
(Desktop: presentation, draft fencing, typed IPC, and human request/decision surfaces; it owns no) t
(authoritative state and stores bearer material only in the Electron main process.) b
(Control: tenant-scoped mutations, expected revisions, idempotency, grants, leases, budgets, event and) t
(replay records in one transaction. Approval is intent; it does not dispatch.) b
(Astra: durable provider-disabled conversations/proposals and one bounded Explain-status protocol. It) t
(cannot approve, grant, dispatch, invoke a model/provider, run a shell, load skills, or use OpenCode.) b
(Worker: uses an already-issued package; private journals persist intent before effects and preserve) t
(unknown outcomes. It cannot self-register, create human authority, or turn exit into scientific truth.) b
(OpenCode: optional pinned harness, not authority. Prompt/tool/MCP/provider-auth activity is upstream) t
(observation only; abort acknowledgement does not establish provider termination.) b
(Kubernetes/provisioner: explicit target identity and narrow operator plans; no ambient current-context) t
(fallback. Setup, attachment, Secret delivery, dispatch, and destructive cleanup are distinct.) b
rule
(Trust and authority boundaries) h
(Human session -> control API: tenant, project, revision, and idempotency checks. Worker identity is) t
(separate from a human login. Agent credentials are scoped, expiring, project-bound control credentials.) t
(Control -> worker: grant/lease/epoch/package constraints; rechecked at lease, renewal, input, start,) t
(observation, and cancellation boundaries. Worker -> provider is not yet a real provider implementation.) t
(Renderer -> main: sender-validated operation-specific IPC; no Node access, privileged generic bridge,) t
(or renderer-held secrets. Artifacts and external inputs are untrusted.) t
endpage

