(Desktop and UI flow) title
(The desktop is a safe client of an independently running control plane, even when co-located.) subtitle
(Connection and read flow) h
(1. A named connection supplies endpoint, identity, organization, compatibility, and health context.) b
(2. Electron main holds the credential in memory and performs HTTP. The sandboxed renderer uses narrow) b
(   IPC and clears in-flight reads, drafts, cached context, and pending commands on connection/project) t
(   changes so a stale response cannot cross a connection boundary.) t
(3. The UI reads projects, plans, decisions, conversations, labbook ledgers, experiments, evidence, and) b
(   recovered history. Held recovery is visibly read-only; browsing never starts work.) t
rule
(User-facing workbench) h
(Projects and plans: immutable plan revisions and approval records are rendered as records, not launch) t
(controls. Human decision resolution is revision-bound intent only; it does not issue a grant or spend.) t
(Conversation: ordinary interaction threads preserve sender, intent, context, and delivery status.) t
(Coordinator workbench: Discuss, Draft experiment, Explain status, and Review results modes create) t
(typed, provider-disabled Astra turns. Selected task/experiment revision chips are explicit. The UI) t
(does not expose raw harness/session identifiers and disables command controls when stale/offline/held.) t
(Research ledger: create studies, register variants, record explicitly manual/imported outcomes, assess) t
(sources, make candidate findings, accept/reaffirm/narrow/supersede/retract with human action, and export) t
(a complete bounded study JSON envelope. These are evidence and judgment records, not automatic science.) t
