(1. Adopt a classified snapshot and create a reviewed destination-specific release.) b
(2. Create/revise an immutable task plan; approve its exact revision and digest. A plan change invalidates) b
(   earlier approval. Configure project currency/exposure/concurrency limits.) t
(3. A human issues a grant for the exact task, worker, snapshot, release, pinned image, budget, expiry,) b
(   and explicit acknowledgement of unmeasured local infrastructure. The worker heartbeats and acquires) t
(   one short lease with a hard deadline; epochs fence stale/revoked work.) t
(4. Before an executable local CPU package returns, external-operation intent records stable operation and) b
(   Docker lookup identities, package/request digests, profile/adapter versions, desired state, and the) t
(   manual-reconciliation retry class. A replay returns the same identity, not a second submit.) t
rule
(Transaction and state semantics) h
(Store._mutate performs authorization, revision/response consistency, state mutation, ordered event, and) t
(idempotency response in one SQLite transaction. Reuse of a key with different content conflicts. Reads) t
(are tenant/project scoped; list bounds are enforced. Consumer/outbox behavior is designed for dedupe.) t
(Grant revoke changes desired state to cancel_requested and advances the epoch; it is not a provider call.) t
(Current reconciliation combines attributed worker and fake-receipt observations by observed time. A later) t
(or equal-time unknown/running/unconfirmed observation blocks terminal reconciliation and preserves exposure.) t
(The data model deliberately separates session, experiment, attempt, external operation, artifact/measurement,) t
(and conclusion lifetimes. A completion, receipt, or evidence hash cannot imply a scientific conclusion.) t
rule
(What is and is not implemented) h
(Implemented bounded control records: projects, credentials, plans/revisions, approvals, input releases,) t
(limits, grants, leases, operation intents, observations, research ledger, interaction, artifacts, and) t
(recovery. ExecutionStore explicitly exposes execution_dispatched=false for its base local records.) t
(Not complete: real provider submission/accounting, production identity/organization login, PostgreSQL or) t
(multi-writer deployment, universal cost caps, full outbox consumers, and an accepted pilot workflow.) t
rule
(Evidence) sh
(src/tessera_control/store.py, api.py, execution.py, execution_api.py, external_operations.py,) t
(runtime_packages.py, input_delivery.py, workers.py, models.py; tests/test_execution*.py, test_plans.py,) t
(test_fake_provider_dispatch.py, test_integrated_experiment_workflow.py.) t
