(CPU and Kubernetes execution flow) title
(Execution is controlled as a bounded, recoverable operation; live provider execution is not enabled.) subtitle
(Local CPU development profile) h
(development-local-cpu-v1 is an opt-in native one-shot worker profile around a control-issued local-cpu-v1) t
(package. It validates a pinned Docker identity, read-only released inputs, private worker credential, grant,) t
(lease and epoch. CpuSupervisor owns a private journal and persists start intent before Docker start. On) t
(lost start/observe/cancel reporting it marks the operation uncertain and reconciles the same identity; it) t
(does not issue a replacement start. It rechecks authority and bounded duration and records cancellation) t
(as requested/unresolved/confirmed only when a matching termination observation confirms it.) t
rule
(CPU safety posture) sh
(The fixture profile uses non-root execution, read-only root, no network, bounded CPU/RAM/scratch/processes,) t
(pinned image, no host mounts, no automatic restart/pull, and read-only input mounts. It is development) t
(evidence, not a supported persistent-output or research-pilot backend.) t
rule
(Kubernetes seams) h
(KubernetesExecutionAdapter accepts only an admitted, provider-disabled package and injected callbacks. It) t
(pins package digest, operation/attempt/lease/epoch, image, workload, target cluster/namespace/PVC identity,) t
(and network-policy evidence. It persists local intent before a deterministic Job create; lost replies use) t
(lookup/reconciliation, never a second Job. Cancellation preserves Job UID and requires fresh Job/owned-Pod) t
(absence to establish termination evidence. Collection handoff emits metadata only; it does not move bytes.) t
(KubernetesDispatchWorkerService consumes a human-approved v36 outbox claim after complete active-grant) t
(predicate rechecks. It durably journals claim, descriptor, reports, and actions, observes/cancels existing) t
(work after lost authority, and never uses Kubernetes credentials/target discovery itself.) t
rule
(Operator setup and conformance) h
(Astra operator setup v2 is a separate, explicit Docker Desktop setup boundary. It requires an absolute) t
(kubeconfig and docker-desktop context and applies only a retained Namespace, deny-all NetworkPolicy, and) t
(64 MiB PVC after explicit plan-digest approval. It does not attach a target, run a workload, create a) t
(Secret, enroll a worker, activate a provider, or delete resources.) t
(The opt-in quota/network conformance probe creates a separate run-labelled namespace/PVC/pods/policies.) t
(It requires declared quota annotations and records actual ENOSPC/EDQUOT evidence or reports unsupported.) t
rule
(Evidence) sh
(src/tessera_worker/cpu.py, supervisor.py, development_runtime.py, kubernetes_*.py, docker_desktop_kubernetes.py;) t
