(Worker upload validates a declared relative path, exact operation/lease/epoch, content digest, per-file and) t
(cumulative bounds. Resumable chunks reserve the same output budget and retain progress after a lost reply.) t
(Artifacts remain quarantined/unclassified, including attributable late output. A complete immutable manifest) t
(requires exactly the approved output set and rechecks retained bytes.) t
(Development output storage reserves userspace bytes/inodes in a private marked workspace, seals only declared) t
(safe nodes after fresh matching confirmed termination, transfers the sealed set, and cleans only after durable) t
(project placement. This is a synthetic/development seam, not the required Linux enforcement backend.) t
rule
(Private project persistence) h
(The local filesystem backend receives bytes from control, not worker paths or storage credentials. It uses) t
(hashed tenant/project/object namespaces, no-overwrite stage/link publication, reconciliation, checksums, and) t
(retention metadata. Placement is not classification, public download, result acceptance, cost settlement, or) t
(provider/scientific success. S3/IAM/KMS, public URLs, external export/move, and production activation remain) t
(unimplemented. Deletion is manual and fail-closed for held/referenced/checkpointed/accepted custody.) t
rule
(Recovery) h
(Backup uses SQLite online copy plus a format-v2 object bundle when committed filesystem objects exist. It) t
(validates exact trusted schema/triggers, foreign keys, object identity/checksum, bounded size/object/time) t
(limits, and publishes a manifest. Restore rejects unsafe/altered input, creates a new owner, revokes all) t
(copied credentials, and enters permanent held_restore. Reads and desktop browsing are allowed; all mutations,) t
(dispatch, renewals, replay, cleanup, target bootstrap, Secret materialization, and provider reconciliation are) t
(refused. Original service/workers/jobs are not stopped or fenced by restore.) t
rule
(Open work) sh
(Automatic container output collection awaits verified persistent Linux storage with hard byte/inode quota,) t
(mount/custody/noexec constraints, container exhaustion, exit, restart, and replay evidence. macOS Docker) t
(Desktop was explicitly found insufficient for the required noexec output profile.) t
