(Environment profiles, offline behavior, cancellation, and security) title
(Profiles are intentionally explicit so ambient machine state cannot become research authority.) subtitle
(Environment/profile matrix) h
(Local developer: supported development workflow is Python 3.11+, uv.lock and Docker Compose/native fixtures.) b
(Compose publishes control only to 127.0.0.1; test has no network. This is not a deployment claim.) t
(Development local CPU: opt-in, pinned image, synthetic fake provider and quarantine-only outputs.) b
(OpenCode: source-inspected v1.18.30 context contract and in-process/HTTP-SSE seams; no selected real server) b
(or recorded compatibility result. Real fixture is opt-in and requires exact executable/version/schema pins.) t
(Kubernetes: fake-client contracts and opt-in Docker Desktop fixtures use explicit target facts; no supported) b
(target attachment, live Kubernetes client path, credential delivery, OpenCode activation, or result acceptance.) t
(Remote OAuth fixtures: v1 one-call and v2 ten-turn scripts are default-disabled retained operational harnesses.) b
(They require a pre-existing remote runner/deployment, opaque owner-bound runtime reference, explicit preflight,) t
(digest-bound confirmation, exact image/target, bounded calls/tokens/time, and no API-key/fallback/top-up path.) t
rule
(Offline, reconnect, and cancellation) h
(The design requires desktop disconnection to leave independent backend and eligible work running under bounded) t
(policy; local source contains a remote-workflow lifecycle and a two-process synthetic reconnect fixture only.) t
(If the control plane is unreachable, workers do not expand grants and preserve unknown state. Reconnect binds) t
(to the same operation, lease, epoch and checkpoint sequence. Unknown control/provider effects block unsafe) t
(replacement. Offline desktop edits are drafts, never approvals or assumed cancellations.) t
(Cancellation distinguishes desired request, delivery, action fence, writer quiescence, provider termination,) t
(credential expiry/revocation, workspace, and charge reconciliation. Current projections only establish request,) t
(unresolved/unknown, or worker-confirmed termination from attributed observations. No green stop badge is) t
(justified by an abort acknowledgement or local terminal state alone.) t
rule
(Security posture and gaps) h
(Implemented/explicit: tenant checks at access; scoped expiring credentials; separate human/agent/worker) t
(identities; revision/epoch fences; loopback local service; browser-origin rejection; hashed private object) t
(names; no raw secrets in records/events/diagnostics; opaque metadata-only credential leases and fake handles;) t
(private journals; input/output path checks; renderer isolation; untrusted artifact treatment; held recovery.) t
(Missing/not proven: production organization authentication/rotation, cryptographic worker build trust and) t
(capability attestation, production secret backend/delivery, selected TLS remote control deployment, provider) t
(cost/termination reconciliation, signed desktop/package updates, storage enforcement, and production monitoring.) t
endpage

